          ],
          "text": "Jerusalem–Jericho road: a steep, stony track descending through the arid Judean wilderness from the hill city toward the low Jordan valley. Rocky limestone ridges and gullies line the way, with dry scrub, scattered acacia and thorn, and patches of wild grass. Rough boulders and cairns mark the path, and distant terraced hills and the faint outline of a walled town lie ahead in the desert haze."
